WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.997
This is Coding Exercise 1.

00:00:01.997 --> 00:00:05.567
Your task is to return patients who have admissions.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:10.127
The output needs patient ID, patient name, admission ID, diagnosis, and department.

00:00:10.127 --> 00:00:15.372
The wording tells you that a match is required.

00:00:15.372 --> 00:00:18.477
We are not trying to keep patients with no admissions.

00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:20.637
That points toward INNER JOIN.

00:00:20.637 --> 00:00:24.692
Start with patients as p and admissions as a.

00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:29.162
Ask what connects them. The relationship is patient_id.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:34.582
Then select the requested columns and sort the result so it is easy to inspect.

00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:37.532
Do not try to force one row per patient.

00:00:37.532 --> 00:00:40.862
The correct grain is one row per matching admission.

00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:45.822
If a patient has three admissions, that patient should appear three times.

00:00:45.822 --> 00:00:50.657
Before using Run and Check, predict whether any patient will disappear.

00:00:50.657 --> 00:00:54.952
After running, compare the number of rows with the number of admissions.

00:00:54.952 --> 00:01:00.022
If the query runs but does not pass, inspect the grain, selected columns,

00:01:00.022 --> 00:01:03.336
and matching condition before randomly editing syntax.
